  "architectural_summary": "**Architectural Summary: WXT**\n\n**1. Overall Architecture Pattern**  \nThis is a **monorepo** (managed via `packages/`) containing a **framework and toolchain** for building browser extensions. It follows a **modular plugin architecture** where core functionality is extended via modules (e.g., `module-react`, `module-vue`). The framework itself is a **build-time tool** (no runtime server), generating extension bundles.\n\n**2. Tech Stack**  \n- **Core**: TypeScript, Vite (implied from `wxt.config.ts`), Vitest (testing).  \n- **UI Frameworks**: React, Vue, Svelte, Solid (via dedicated modules).  \n- **Tooling**: CLI (`wxt-*` commands), custom modules (`analytics`, `i18n`, `storage`).  \n- **Infrastructure**: GitHub Actions for CI/CD (multiple workflows), no containerization or cloud provider specified.\n\n**3. API Surface**  \nNo traditional web API routes. Instead, the framework exposes a **CLI interface** (`wxt build`, `wxt init`, etc.) and **module APIs** for extension development (e.g., `storage`, `i18n`). Entrypoints (`packages/*/entrypoints/`) define extension components (popup, content scripts).\n\n**4. Data Layer**  \nNo persistent databases. The `storage` package provides wrappers for browser extension storage APIs (e.g., `chrome.storage`). Data models are extension-specific, with no ORM.\n\n**5. Infrastructure Maturity**  \n- **CI/CD**: Robust GitHub Actions setup (`validate`, `release`, `publish-docs`, etc.).  \n- **Deployment**: Packages published to npm; documentation deployed via `publish-docs.yml`.  \n- **Testing**: Vitest used across packages (e.g., `vitest.config.ts` in `runner`, `i18n`).  \n- **Containerization**: None—tooling runs locally or in CI.\n\n**6. Strengths**  \n- **Well-structured monorepo**: Clear separation of concerns (`packages/` for core, modules, and examples).  \n- **Extensible design**: Modules (`module-*`) allow framework-agnostic UI development.  \n- **Comprehensive tooling**: CLI, testing, and automation workflows cover the full extension lifecycle.  \n- **Documentation**: Detailed guides (`docs/guide/`) and API docs (`docs/api/cli/`).\n\n**7. Weaknesses / Gaps**  \n- **No containerization**: Limits reproducibility for complex build environments.  \n- **Tight coupling to Vite**: Could hinder adoption if alternative bundlers are needed.  \n- **Limited infrastructure visibility**: No deployment or monitoring details for hosted services (if any).  \n- **Testing gaps**: Some packages (e.g., `auto-icons`) have tests, but coverage is unclear.",
